  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 602 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nThe relentless summer heat will continue through the end of July \nwith triple-digit high temperatures as ridging aloft prevails. Heat \nindex values are expected to be higher than earlier this week as \nwell as humidity increases via persistent low level southerly to \nsoutheasterly flow. Heat headlines may be needed as heat index \nvalues approach 108-110 degrees Saturday afternoon, mainly along and \neast of the I-35 corridor.\n\nThere will be a limited opportunity for isolated to scattered \nshowers and storms across portions of South Central Texas. The \naforementioned ridge aloft is expected to shift west over the Desert \nSouthwest, placing our region beneath northwesterly flow.\nThis will allow for a weak frontal boundary to track across South \nCentral Texas late this weekend. However, there are still \ndiscrepancies on the timing of this weak boundary among \ndeterministic guidance on any convective development over the \nweekend, and most precipitation chances are capped at 30% or less\nfor late Saturday afternoon and Sunday. More seasonable \ntemperatures return Sunday and into early next week.",
